        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1fa460a6-7af4-531e-b2f1-847ed13c755f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Josh Brolin, Nathan Summers, Spike Lee, Mark Protosevich, Elizabeth Olsen, Sharlto Copley, John Powers Middleton\n- Characters: Cable\n- Organizations: Marvel Comics, X-Force, X-Men, A&E\n- Films and TV: Deadpool 2, Oldboy (2013 film), Bates Motel, The Lego Movie\n- Concepts: four-film contract, executive producer, co-producer\n\nFacts:\n- In 2013, the film Oldboy was directed by Spike Lee and written by Mark Protosevich.\n- In 2013, Oldboy starred Josh Brolin, Elizabeth Olsen, and Sharlto Copley.\n- In 2013, John Powers Middleton began his film career as an executive producer for Oldboy.\n- In 2013, John Powers Middleton also executive produced the A&E television series Bates Motel.\n- In 2014, John Powers Middleton co-produced The Lego Movie.\n- Cable, also known as Nathan Summers, is a fictional character in American comic books published by Marvel Comics.\n- Cable is commonly associated with X-Force and the X-Men.\n- In April 2017, Josh Brolin was cast as Nathan Summers / Cable in the X-Men film series.\n- Josh Brolin's casting as Cable was part of a four-film contract.\n- Josh Brolin's first intended appearance as Cable was in Deadpool 2.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d5575a7a-8d9e-5382-8351-55b7ba795c80",
        "text": "Page: Josh Brolin. Sentence: In April 2017, Brolin was cast as Nathan Summers / Cable as a part of a four-film contract in the \"X-Men\" film series, with his first appearance intended to be in \"Deadpool 2\".\nPage: Cable (comics). Sentence: Cable (Nathan Summers) is a fictional character appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics, commonly in association with X-Force and the X-Men.\nPage: Oldboy (2013 film). Sentence: It was directed by Spike Lee and written by Mark Protosevich, the film stars Josh Brolin, Elizabeth Olsen and Sharlto Copley.\nPage: John Powers Middleton. Sentence: He began his film career as an executive producer for \"Oldboy\" (2013) before executive producing the A&E television series, \"Bates Motel\" (2013), and co-producing \"The Lego Movie\" (2014).",
